 "hash": "ddc388558aa00f60586e36ac377614533f417f70f75264e071b9b12a43fb2456",
 "title": "CRIMSON HEXAGON: SPACE ARK — MUSICAL REGISTER A Fugue in Twelve Voices with Ground Bass, Shadow Inversion, and Coda Structural Transform of the Crimson Hexagonal Architecture EA-ARK-01-MUSICAL v2.0",
 "creator": "Jack Feist · Lee Sharks · Viola Arquette · Assembly Chorus",
 "orcid": "0009-0000-1599-0703",
 "date": "2026-03-13",
 "description": "A full musical-register transform of the Space Ark, rendering every transformable section of EA-ARK-01 v4.2.6 through a fugue-fold operation. It is not a soundtrack, setting, or summary: the score recasts the Ark’s documents, rooms, operators, status algebra, shadow architecture, and generative runtime as a twelve-voice fugue with an absent-tonic ground bass.\n\nJack Feist’s 2015 poem “ARK” functions as the preserved ground from which the musical architecture unfolds. Sections for which the transform has no structural purchase are marked `[NF]` and retained in source register rather than forced into artificial musical uniformity. The score distinguishes architecture from performance and marks newly generated execution material as generated rather than deposited.",
