   "reason": "DW-003 intake (LABOR-prepared, TACHYON-verified: AXN match + factual probes vs record body)",
   "was": "\"CRIMSON HEXAGON\" is a creative work by Lee Sharks · Jack Feist in the Crimson Hexagonal Archive, dated 2026-03-13. A Fugue in Twelve Voices with Ground Bass, Shadow Inversion, and Coda. The work comprises 46,380 words and is classified under the GENERATIVE family. The work was removed from Zenodo o",
   "now": "A full musical-register transform of the Space Ark, rendering every transformable section of EA-ARK-01 v4.2.6 through a fugue-fold operation. It is not a soundtrack, setting, or summary: the score recasts the Ark’s documents, rooms, operators, status algebra, shadow architecture, and generative runtime as a twelve-voice fugue with an absent-tonic ground bass.\n\nJack Feist’s 2015 poem “ARK” functions as the preserved ground from which the musical architecture unfolds. Sections for which the transform has no structural purchase are marked `[NF]` and retained in source register rather than forced into artificial musical uniformity. The score distinguishes architecture from performance and marks newly generated execution material as generated rather than deposited."
  },
